# Internal sales playbook layer — repo and site are PUBLIC; this never ships.
#
# This rule used to read `docs/internal/` alone, which never matched the
# playbook's actual path, so content/gcp-playbook.md was tracked and public.
# It remains in git history: this rule plus the accompanying `git rm --cached`
# only stop it shipping from here forward.
#
# The file must still exist LOCALLY on any machine that runs the pipeline:
# scripts/generate-briefing.js feeds it to Stage 4b as ground truth for "Our
# Play", and scripts/generate-weekly.sh reads its "Last verified" date for the
# 90-day staleness warning. Both degrade to a warning when it is missing, so a
# fresh clone still builds — it just drafts Our Play without ground truth.
docs/internal/
content/gcp-playbook.md
